1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,440
Noticed more hair coming out in the shower since starting Ozempic, Wegovy, or Mounjaro?

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:17,280
Clinical trials confirm this — hair loss showed up in about 3% of Wegovy users versus 1% on placebo, and up to 5.7% on Mounjaro versus under 1% on placebo.

3
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:24,640
Three things drive it: rapid weight loss itself, nutrient gaps from eating less, and nausea that blocks absorption.

4
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,840
First, losing weight quickly shocks your system.

5
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:38,560
Your body redirects energy away from non-essential functions like hair growth, and follicles that were actively growing shift into a resting phase all at once — that's the sudden shedding.

6
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:44,160
Second, a smaller appetite means less protein, iron, and zinc reaching your follicles.

7
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:48,720
Without those building blocks, hair grows in thinner and falls out faster.

8
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:56,560
Third, the nausea common with these medications means even the food you do eat doesn't get fully absorbed, worsening the nutrient gap.

9
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:02,640
Slow your rate of weight loss and prioritize protein, iron, and zinc-rich foods to help follicles recover.

10
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:09,680
Growth typically resumes once weight stabilizes — talk to your doctor about adjusting your dose rather than stopping on your own.
